  "details": "I've been working on a project with various constructions of constraints. One of them is a contact tracker that tracks players when it comes in contact with someone.\n\nThe problem presists in when after using it for the first time on someone and it loses tracking, it freezes in place. Even though I didn't animate to do that. But the moment I toggle it and try again after the manual reset, it seems to work as intended, without a problem. The moment I reset / reload my avatar, that first time using it will break, until i toggle it on and off.\n\nI can recreate this happening like 90% of the time.\n\nThis problem does not happen in Unity itself, since I'm still using the normal Constraints from Unity. I assume it happens ingame, since it converts them to the VRCConstraints.\n\nThe link below leads you to an unlisted video\n\n(The white cube is attached to the Contact tracker for debugging)\n\n(The ID of the avatar used in the video is: avtr_f5c9a520-da6f-48ee-a92b-dcf2284e9af9)\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=tMgNoY0gcU0",
